:: ConfessionToHusband
<h2 class="story-title">The Confession</h2>

The sethani thought to herself: *This affair was bound to be revealed sometime. Why commit an unkarmic deed by hiding it? If she wanted, she could deceive her husband, but she didn't have the heart to.*

She told him the whole story right from the beginning—about the thakur, the tunnel, the adoption, the thief. Every detail of her near-betrayal.

The seth listened in silence.

When she finished, he felt as if the pot of hot milk had been rescued just as the curd starter was about to fall into it. Good thing, too. The mistake was certainly his—he had completely ignored his very own Lakshmi and headed off to distant lands to make money.

"You've told me the complete truth," he said. "And so I forgive you."

